cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Buying back communication with retrieval compute in federated
  fine-tuning: code and experiment logs
message: >-
  If you use this software or its experiment logs, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Jeonghun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3486-5590"
    affiliation: Macquarie University
repository-code: "https://github.com/hufs0529/rag-fl"
abstract: >-
  Code, experiment logs and analysis scripts for a six-week STEM
  research placement testing whether client-side retrieval compute
  can buy back communication in federated LLM fine-tuning. Twenty-four
  federated runs of SmolLM2-135M with LoRA adapters on Natural
  Questions were trained under an identical 1.74 GB communication
  budget, varying only cross-encoder reranking depth over six levels
  with four seeds. Reranking depth demonstrably changed which
  documents reached the prompt but did not reduce rounds to target;
  the break is located at the link between document quality and
  learning.
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - parameter-efficient fine-tuning
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - reranking
  - communication efficiency
  - large language models
license: Apache-2.0
